# CODEOWNERS for <org>/[[ .TenantName ]]-gitops
#
# The second of two repositories (the machine repo). Kept separate from the
# apps+infra source repo because ArgoCD reads this repo, and CI bots write
# rendered manifests to it. It is the one repo where automation holds credentials.
#
# In this monorepo its root is 3-tenant-workloads/[[ .TenantName ]]/gitops/; when the
# tree is split out (git filter-repo) it becomes the real repository root unchanged.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the general rule goes first.

# The team owns its own workloads: per-env values.yaml and CI-rendered manifests.
[[- range .Owners ]]
*                                       @acme-corp/[[ . ]]
[[- end ]]

# The tenancy boundary and ArgoCD wiring are platform-owned. A team cannot widen its
# own AppProject, relax its NetworkPolicy, or repoint its ApplicationSet.
/platform/                              @acme-corp/platform-engineering

# Kyverno exceptions weaken a cluster-wide guardrail, so security signs those off.
/platform/team/policy-exceptions.yaml   @acme-corp/security
